  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed signage, by reason of&amp;nbsp;prominent siting, inappropriate external finish materials and internal illumination, would result in a structure with an obtrusive appearance. This would be inappropriate within the immediate streetscene and would therefore fail to preserve the character and appearance of the conservation area and the setting of the adjacent listed buildings, without clear and convincing justification nor public benefits to outweigh the harm. The proposal is therefore contrary to Sections 66 and 72 of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policies HC1 C of the London Plan (2021), Core Strategy (2012), and policies DM5 and DM7 of the Development Management Policies Local plan (2013) and GR1 of the Draft Harrow Local Plan 2021-2044.&lt;/p&gt;"
